=== Translation to L'(1/2,f) on odd subfamily ===

Note: KMV eq. (5) gives unmollified harmonic 2nd moment of
Lambda^(k)(f,1/2) over ALL of S_2*(q) as ~ c'_k (log qhat)^{2k+1}.
For k=1: power is (log qhat)^3.

On odd subfamily, |Lambda'(1/2,f)|^2 = qhat * |L'(1/2,f)|^2.
On even subfamily, |Lambda'(1/2,f)|^2 = qhat * |log(qhat)*L(1/2,f) + ...|^2,
which is (log qhat)^2 * |L(1/2,f)|^2 to leading order, contributing
(log qhat)^2 * (log qhat)  = (log qhat)^3 from the L^2 average ~ log qhat.

Hence the (log qhat)^3 leading total in eq. (5) comes from BOTH subfamilies.

On odd subfamily ALONE, sum^h |L'(1/2,f)|^2 has leading order
at most (log qhat)^3, NOT (log qhat)^4 as the S4 chain claims.

